<DocsLayout title="Source map" subtitle="Implementation entry points for tracing behavior and making focused changes." description="Implementation entry points for tracing behavior and making focused changes." toc={toc}>
  <section id="geometry" class="doc-section">
    <h2>CAD and drawing</h2>
    <p>Begin at <code>packages/core/src/index.ts</code> to see namespace exports. <code>packages/core/src/cad/index.ts</code> lists CAD APIs; <code>packages/core/src/drawing/index.ts</code> lists drawing operations.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>cad/sketch.ts</code>, <code>sketch-shapes.ts</code>, <code>snap.ts</code>, <code>intersect.ts</code>: sketch data, shapes, snapping, and intersection.</li>
      <li><code>cad/history.ts</code>, <code>history-edit.ts</code>, <code>history-brep.ts</code>: feature history, edits, and B-rep reconstruction.</li>
      <li><code>cad/brep/</code>, <code>solid.ts</code>, <code>tessellate.ts</code>: solid topology, modelling, and renderable meshes.</li>
      <li><code>cad/import-step.ts</code>, <code>dxf.ts</code>, and <code>import-drawing.ts</code>: exchange and import boundaries.</li>
      <li><code>cad/scene-analysis.ts</code>, <code>scene-evidence.ts</code>, <code>dfm.ts</code>: scene analysis, evidence, and manufacturability checks.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Keep import parsing, exact geometry, tessellation, and viewport selection separate when tracing a display issue. A visible mesh may have a different origin from an editable parametric feature.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="cam" class="doc-section">
    <h2>CAM and G-code</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>packages/core/src/cam/index.ts</code>: public CAM namespaces and exports.</li>
      <li><code>cam/operations/</code> and <code>cam/generator/</code>: operation implementations and generation pipeline.</li>
      <li><code>cam/setup.ts</code>, <code>indexing.ts</code>, <code>ir.ts</code>: setup frames, indexed machining, and intermediate motion representation.</li>
      <li><code>cam/post/index.ts</code>, <code>emitter.ts</code>, and the dialect files: registered posts and shared program emission.</li>
      <li><code>cam/post/advanced/</code>: advanced G-code transformations and controller-oriented output handling.</li>
      <li><code>cam/verify/</code>, <code>kernel/</code>, <code>model/</code>, and <code>viewer/</code>: verification, machining kernels, models, and viewer helpers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Trace persisted machining through <code>apps/sidecar/src/http/toolpaths.ts</code> and <code>src/services/cam-program.ts</code>, then into the desktop CAM feature. The <a href="/docs/setups">setups reference</a> explains how portable program documents relate to saved toolpaths.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="http" class="doc-section">
    <h2>HTTP and persistence</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>packages/api/src/index.ts</code>, <code>groups/</code>, <code>errors.ts</code>, <code>auth.ts</code>: endpoint contracts, wire errors, and authorization declarations.</li>
      <li><code>packages/api/src/client.ts</code>: full contract-based Effect client with bearer middleware.</li>
      <li><code>packages/api/scripts/generate-clients.ts</code>: target outputs and explicit generation exclusions.</li>
      <li><code>packages/httpapi-codegen/src/index.ts</code>: contract reflection, validation, and client emitters.</li>
      <li><code>apps/sidecar/src/main.ts</code>, <code>config.ts</code>, <code>layers.ts</code>: server lifecycle, configuration, and dependency wiring.</li>
      <li><code>apps/sidecar/src/http/</code>, <code>services/</code>, <code>repos/</code>: protocol adapters, application operations, and persistence access.</li>
      <li><code>packages/db/src/index.ts</code>, <code>schema.ts</code>, <code>upgrade.ts</code>, <code>migrate.ts</code>: database service, tables, upgrade safety, and CLI.</li>
      <li><code>packages/db/drizzle/</code>: generated migrations and metadata shipped with the desktop.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="clients" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Desktop and mobile</h2>
    <p><code>apps/desktop/src/app/App.tsx</code>, <code>Shell.tsx</code>, and <code>routes.tsx</code> assemble the workbench and routes. <code>client.ts</code> and <code>sidecar.ts</code> handle API access and native connection state. Product behavior lives under <code>src/features</code>; shared controls and state live under <code>src/shared</code>.</p>
    <p>The viewport is under <code>apps/desktop/src/viewport</code>, split into <code>editor2d</code>, <code>view3d</code>, and <code>spatial</code>. Native commands and lifecycle are under <code>apps/desktop/src-tauri/src</code>; packaging configuration is <code>src-tauri/tauri.conf.json</code>.</p>
    <p>Mobile routes are under <code>apps/mobile/app</code>, reusable components under <code>components</code>, and client/pairing logic under <code>lib</code>. The native socket module is <code>modules/companion-net</code>. On the server, start companion tracing at <code>apps/sidecar/src/http/companion.ts</code> and <code>services/companion.ts</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="automation" class="doc-section">
    <h2>AI, plugins, history, and workflows</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>packages/ai/src/actions</code> and <code>tools</code>: action declarations and assistant tool integration.</li>
      <li><code>packages/ai/src/nikcli</code>, <code>prompts</code>, and <code>skills</code>: embedded host integration and assistant guidance.</li>
      <li><code>apps/sidecar/src/services/ai.ts</code>: live AI dependencies and host selection.</li>
      <li><code>packages/nikcli-plugin/src/index.ts</code>: external nikcli HTTP bridge.</li>
      <li><code>packages/plugin-sdk/src/index.ts</code> and <code>apps/sidecar/src/plugins/host.ts</code>: plugin authoring surface and runtime host.</li>
      <li><code>packages/vcs/src/index.ts</code>, <code>apps/sidecar/src/services/project-vcs.ts</code>, and <code>repos/project-vcs-repo.ts</code>: history library, orchestration, and persistence.</li>
      <li><code>packages/workflow/src/index.ts</code>, <code>apps/sidecar/src/services/workflow-runner.ts</code>, and <code>workflow-service-steps-live.ts</code>: workflow contract, execution, and service step registration.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Version control lives in <code>packages/vcs/src</code>: <code>object.ts</code> (git object format), <code>repository.ts</code> (refs and commits), <code>snapshot.ts</code>, <code>diff.ts</code>, <code>store.ts</code>, <code>transport.ts</code>, and <code>github.ts</code>. Workflows live in <code>packages/workflow/src</code>: <code>schema.ts</code>, <code>trigger.ts</code> (glob and trigger matching), and <code>run.ts</code>. Workflow files are read from <code>.cadcamfun/workflows/</code> in the project tree.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="web" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Documentation and delivery</h2>
    <p><code>packages/web/src/pages/docs</code> contains the documentation articles. <code>src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro</code> provides the shared article shell. Navigation and retrieval copy are in <code>src/data/docsSidebar.ts</code> and <code>docsIndex.ts</code>; shared package descriptions are in <code>architecture.ts</code>.</p>
    <p><code>src/lib/docsMarkdown.ts</code> converts rendered articles to Markdown for <code>src/pages/llm.ts</code> and the documentation assistant. Retrieval is in <code>docsRetrieval.ts</code>; assistant execution is in <code>src/pages/api/docs-assistant.ts</code>. Artifact parsing and storage helpers are in <code>src/lib/docsArtifact.ts</code>.</p>
    <p><code>packages/web/script/dev.ts</code> starts Astro and the local Studio process. <code>studio-server.ts</code> owns the local SQLite overview API. <code>astro.config.mjs</code> configures prerendering infrastructure and the local proxy; <code>wrangler.toml</code> declares Worker bindings.</p>
    <p>Desktop compilation and release staging start in <code>scripts/build.ts</code>. CI and release workflows are under <code>.github/workflows</code>. See <a href="/docs/release">Release and updates</a> for artifact generation and signing requirements.</p>
  </section>


  <section id="trace-a-request" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Trace behavior across boundaries</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Identify the endpoint in the <a href="/docs/api">resource reference</a> and read its parameter, body, response, and error schemas.</li>
      <li>Locate its HttpApi declaration in the API root composition. Some foundational resources, including projects, live directly under <code>packages/api/src</code>; other groups live under <code>src/groups</code>.</li>
      <li>Find its handler under <code>apps/sidecar/src/http</code>. Read the current-user and resource checks before following its service or repository call.</li>
      <li>For calculation, continue into core. For storage, continue through the repository and <code>Database.query</code>. For provider/network behavior, inspect the configured adapter.</li>
      <li>Return to the desktop or mobile caller and inspect its envelope handling, session state, cancellation, and error display.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>For example, a missing name in project creation is rejected in <code>apps/sidecar/src/http/projects.ts</code>; it is not a SQLite error. A portable CAM document mismatch is checked by <code>apps/sidecar/src/services/cam-program.ts</code>; parsing NC in the viewport cannot bypass it. A paired phone route refusal originates in the companion gateway's method/path policy.</p>
  </section>

